{
  "vectors": "url-normalize",
  "version": 1,
  "spec": "docs/cloudkit-schema-design.md §4.1 (One URL normalizer)",
  "implementations": {
    "swift": "ForeverLMApp/Shared/Sync/Core/URLNormalizer.swift (moved from Shared/Services/Storage in WP2, its local-path branch injected; v1 is frozen as this implementation)",
    "js": "schema/js/url-normalize-v1.js"
  },
  "format": "Each case: input (a stored URL or key); normalized = URLNormalizer.normalize(input) as the Mac computes it; sourceID = \"src_\" + hex(sha256(\"source:v1:\" + normalized)) (SourceIdentity.stableID); iphoneNormalized, present only where it differs, is what the iPhone's MobileURLNormalizer (iOS/MobileCloudMutations.swift) made of the same input, the historical form migration 155 records as an extra url: work key. origin: URLNormalizerTests.<test> (the Mac's own fixtures), edge (one branch of normalize each), stand-in (a made-up URL that takes the branch of a live URL the privacy filter dropped;Local file paths (inputs starting with /) are excluded: they normalize against the Mac's content roots, and the iPhone and the web reject them.",
  "generatedBy": "A standalone build of URLNormalizer.swift and MobileURLNormalizer (macOS 27 Foundation) run over the inputs; regenerate the same way when a branch is added, never by hand.",
  "notes": [
    "v1 strips a bioRxiv or medRxiv DOI's whole last segment (10.1101/2025.04.11.648220v1 becomes 10.1101/2025.04.11), so two preprints posted the same day share one key. It is v1 behaviour and stays frozen here; a fix is a v2 rule for new keys only (§4.1).",
    "The private repository also pins about 2,100 live URLs from a real library; they are left out here."
  ],
